{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463570-faverite-use-for-a-demesne","id":1463570,"title":"Faverite use for a Demesne","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-12T04:10:42-07:00","id":1463570,"title":"Faverite use for a Demesne","content":"I always look at the Demesne background and I'm never sure what to do with it. I think it's conceptially really cool, but mechanically a bit.... EH. As you don't really need it to do cool stuff with mind.<br /> <br /> So whats your favierite thing to do with a Demesne? Or what cool things have you done with the background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","name":"Jasper mage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T06:06:02-07:00","id":1463582,"title":"","content":"I think some of it depends on the storyteller, but I had an Akashic Brother who would use Mind to commit the text of many many books to memory, and store them in his Demesne. In this way, he gained a Library background rating. Added to this, almost every time he slept, he would enter his Demesne (he also had the Lucid Dreaming talent, though it's not strictly necessary) and he would study. For him, no time was ever wasted just sleeping - in the waking hours he would do physical things like train and kick ass, and while he was sleeping he would study and gain knowledge in his Demesne.<br /> <br /> If you can pull others into your Demesne, you can use it as an extremely secure place to have discussions or to do things to their subconscious sleeping minds that might otherwise be impossible. If you can pull an otherwise unbeatable enemy there, you may be able to destroy them because within your own Demesne you have godlike power. It's essentially your own personal horizon realm that adjusts to your every whim. Bringing others there can carry risk though - you simultaneously give them a way to more easily find it again on their own, and like a Node, such a place has power and someone with sufficient ability may try to take it over for themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 10-12-2021, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T14:54:38-07:00","id":1463625,"title":"","content":"I have a story with an NPC who can access a dream realm very much like a Demesne, but it doesn't perfectly fit the Background description, because the dreamer can access knowledge from outside his own experience about a specific subject (unlike Dream which can be changed from day to day). <br /> <br /> The description says that it exists as a <i>semi-permanent</i> realm in the Maya. Does it disappear when the Mage dies? If so, how soon after?<br /> <br /> If the dreamer shapes the whole realm into a building with windows, can s/he look out the window and see parts of the Maya outside the realm?<br /> <br /> If you equip invited guests with tools, can they assist in building out the realm?<br /> <br /> Rotes with 6 dots or less in Spheres:<br /> <br /> Prime 2, Time 2: Conjure the ideal version of yourself in the dream and ask how s/he became so amazing - the path to follow.<br /> <br /> Prime 2, Matter 2, Life 2: Make food eaten in the dream sustain your sleeping body.<br /> <br /> Mind 3, Forces 3: Give the realm a gravitational effect that holds even the most willful dreamers there. <br /> <br /> Spirit 2: Summon a friendly Spirit who can use the realm while you are awake.<br /> <br /> Mind 3, Data 3: Use a mainframe computer to expand the size of the realm. Duplicate parts of the realm in a fixed state so that they can be experienced in a video game. <br /> <br /> Mind 3, Correspondence 3: Chose a recently published work of fiction by a popular author and scan the world for different dreams readers have, inspired by the same book. <br /> <br /> Mind 1, Prime 1, Entropy 1, Time 2: Analyze a dream to determine your relationship to the experience, the Resonance of the dream and how your actions in the dream change your personal Resonance. Use the Demesne to develop strong personal Resonance without acting in the world.<br /> <br /> Entropy 1, Forces 1: Correctly guess how the word &quot;Demesne&quot; is pronounced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T04:18:18-07:00","id":1463691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463570-faverite-use-for-a-demesne?p=1463625#post1463625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 3, Correspondence 3: Chose a recently published work of fiction by a popular author and scan the world for different dreams readers have, inspired by the same book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you use this to gather rumours? Like you have an idea of an event that has happened and then reach out to find people who might be dreaming about the event because they saw it or heard about it and gained intel?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I once had a mage with a low level one, and I only used it for narrative purposes to exsplore his own trauma (dreamspeaker) and use it as an exscuse for him to grow as a person, because i'd started him at arte 1. I had a whole pintrest album dedicated to what I imagined his Demesne to look like. It was really fun from a RP perspective, but he wasn't really big into mind so I didn't mechanically use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","name":"Jasper mage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T09:32:41-07:00","id":1463710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jasper mage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463570-faverite-use-for-a-demesne?p=1463691#post1463691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use this to gather rumours? Like you have an idea of an event that has happened and then reach out to find people who might be dreaming about the event because they saw it or heard about it and gained intel?</div> </div> </div> </div>By such an effect alone you wouldn't be able to determine why someone is dreaming with an event, but you can surely find out people with dreams inspired by the event. You'll miss on witnesses that aren't dreaming about it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T12:21:44-07:00","id":1463737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jasper mage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463570-faverite-use-for-a-demesne?p=1463691#post1463691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use this to gather rumours? Like you have an idea of an event that has happened and then reach out to find people who might be dreaming about the event because they saw it or heard about it and gained intel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you would get more useful information by scanning for rumors passing between conscious speakers. If a player asked to use this effect, I would give them two options:<br /> <br /> 1. Focus on <i>Content Only</i>, obtaining snippets of conversation passing between vaguely represented speakers that even includes their internal monologue. This avoids Mages in the grapevine detecting the scry.<br /> <br /> 2. The same, but including the <i>Who.</i> If a NWO Mage with Mind/Correspondence is a grape in the vine, they have a a chance to detect the scry and attempt to trace it back to you if they have Corr2. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jasper mage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463570-faverite-use-for-a-demesne?p=1463691#post1463691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once had a mage with a low level one, and I only used it for narrative purposes to exsplore his own trauma (dreamspeaker) and use it as an exscuse for him to grow as a person, because i'd started him at arte 1. I had a whole pintrest album dedicated to what I imagined his Demesne to look like. It was really fun from a RP perspective, but he wasn't really big into mind so I didn't mechanically use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find starting with low Arete punitive. If a player wants to raise a Sphere above their current Arete rating, they have to pay twice. When you are 15 and you have Summer Holidays, I suppose this high XP threshold isn't a problem. My sessions can be infrequent, depending on circumstances. I raised the ceiling on starting Arete to five. It comes at the cost of a lot of perky Backgrounds and Merits. It could be fun to play an Acolyte campaign, where you are bartering for the services of more powerful Mages by doing a lot of mundane tasks. <br /> <br /> IRL, I discovered this amazing tool called the Swish Technique that comes from Neuro-Linguistic Programming. It is incredibly effective at neutralizing the negative emotional content of a past experience. It was a rough patch before I started using Swish and it didn't take that much practice to get onto better footing. <br /> <br /> Story-wise, I have an NPC with some nasty suspicions about things going on in her family that is going to come into play. I have to do it well, though and I am not rushing it. The hints that this is an avenue to be investigated will get increasingly more obvious until the PCs figure it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T14:21:02-07:00","id":1463884,"title":"","content":"I mostly play on a WoD IM chat group. so xp every day baby B)<br /> <br /> but does make a Demesne a questionmark background. because your not sure how useful it'll be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","name":"Jasper mage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:01:32-07:00","id":1463898,"title":"","content":"Demesne is much like Spirit, in that it can either be very useful or pretty useless, depending on the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> One idea I had for a plot a while back is the PC's Demesne gets attacked by astral pirates, so the PC (and whoever they could bring with them) had to fight them off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T15:20:18-07:00","id":1464224,"title":"","content":"A Buddhist Chorister in my game has the Demesne background, and it's become a major aspect of the story over the past several years. It began in the form of a small village with classically Far Eastern inspired features, with her home represented as a small Buddhist temple at the center. Gradually it expanded and began to take on a recognizable form, mirroring New York City (where the chronicle takes place) in its general shape, with large pagodas standing in for skyscrapers and rock gardens and ponds filling in for parks. Manhattan is part town and part mountain, with a winding path that has provided spirit quest landmarks and staging grounds for Works, as well as just a place to get a nice view. The demesne also sometimes incorporates features from the PC's experiences: a school inhabited by dark things where the PC's and allies staged a rescue is in town, while one face of Jupiter is close in the sky.<br /> <br /> Over time, dreamers started to manifest. At first, they would pop in and out, but over time many learned to stay, and because it's a dream realm, they learn to lucidly dream, creating their own mini-realities within the greater environment (the PC is able to nix anything she doesn't like, however). One dreamer even thought she was in Heaven, and took it as a sign that the End Times were nearing, necessitating an encounter in the real world to get her to cool her jets. As the demesne has expanded and more dreamers regularly entered, people in NYC have realized that it's a Real Thing; this understanding went international after the last NYC Comic Con brought thousands of new dreamers from all over into the realm. The Technocracy doesn't really understand what is happening here, but they've been on their back feet ever since Iceland seceded from the Consensus (having renewed their ancient ties to the Fair Folk) a few years ago -- a whole 'nother story.<br /> <br /> On any given night, dreamers manifest their imaginations, with the most skilled able to mimic their favorite superheroes and villains, play Quidditch or Transformers, and so on. No one can die in the dream realm, so blowing up your friends is great fun. There's probably a Mage LARP happening in there somewhere...<br /> <br /> This just scratches the surface of what's been going on in the demesne. The &quot;tree that would be&quot; (the shadow of a Hollow World shrub that manifested in the demesne and just kept growing) and the &quot;soul of Bo&quot; (a rocker whose essence, but not his body, was saved from a Nephandus) have both played large roles in the story, along with many other features. Most significantly, long-time efforts finally achieved a desired result: there now exists a mandala-portal on the mountain that connects the demesne to the Digital Web. <br /> <br /> Later in the year I'll begin what is probably the final story of the chronicle, which began about 10 years ago. The Annunaki (my Antediluvians) have risen, the Fair Folk are returning to take what land and minds they can (humans have just learned about the Goblin Market in NYC), and the forces of Darkness -- while partially thwarted -- still hope to corrupt the world entire. If it comes down to it, the demesne may serve as a failsafe, a place to &quot;upload&quot; as much of humanity as possible if the planet cannot be saved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}